{"name":"Holiday Camp","hex":"#6d9e7a","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"holiday camp","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An enclosed resort providing accommodation (often in chalets) and entertainment, generally aimed at families."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/holiday_camp"}],"entries":[{"title":"Holiday camp","blocks":[{"text":"A holiday camp is a type of holiday accommodation, primarily in the United Kingdom, that encourages holidaymakers to stay within the site boundary, and provides entertainment and facilities for them throughout the day. Since the 1970s, the term has fallen out of favour with terms such as holiday park, resort, holiday village and holiday centre replacing it."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3b/Irl_Butlins_Mosney.jpg/330px-Irl_Butlins_Mosney.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Holiday_camp","wikidata":"Q17006838"},{"title":"Holiday Camp (film)","blocks":[{"text":"Holiday Camp is a 1947 British comedy drama film directed by Ken Annakin, starring Flora Robson, Jack Warner, Dennis Price, and Hazel Court, and also features Kathleen Harrison and Jimmy Hanley. It is set at one of the then-popular holiday camps. It was the first film to feature the Huggett family, who went on to star in The Huggetts film series."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/a/ad/%22Holiday_Camp%22_%281947%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Holiday_Camp_(film)","wikidata":"Q5880372"},{"title":"Holiday","blocks":[{"text":"A holiday is a day or other period of time set aside for festivals or recreation. Public holidays are set by public authorities and vary by state or region. Religious holidays are set by religious organizations for their members and are often also observed as public holidays in religious majority countries. Some religious holidays, such as Christmas, have become secularised by part or all of those who observe them. In addition to secularisation, many holidays have become commercialised due to the growth of industry."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f3/Lathmar_Holi_2022_in_Nandgaon%2C_Uttar_Pradesh_%28edited%29.jpg/330px-Lathmar_Holi_2022_in_Nandgaon%2C_Uttar_Pradesh_%28edited%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Holiday","wikidata":"Q1445650"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/80/Champs-Elysees_Bastille_Day_2013_Paris_t090858.jpg/500px-Champs-Elysees_Bastille_Day_2013_Paris_t090858.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/80/Champs-Elysees_Bastille_Day_2013_Paris_t090858.jpg/1280px-Champs-Elysees_Bastille_Day_2013_Paris_t090858.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/80/Champs-Elysees_Bastille_Day_2013_Paris_t090858.jpg/500px-Champs-Elysees_Bastille_Day_2013_Paris_t090858.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AChamps-Elysees_Bastille_Day_2013_Paris_t090858.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6c/School_Children_On_a_Mission.jpg/500px-School_Children_On_a_Mission.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6c/School_Children_On_a_Mission.jpg/1280px-School_Children_On_a_Mission.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6c/School_Children_On_a_Mission.jpg/500px-School_Children_On_a_Mission.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_